{"name":"Light Freshman","hex":"#ecf4d2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"freshman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a person (of either sex) entering the first year of an institution, especially a high school (ninth grade for US, grade 9 for  Canada, grade 7 for Philippines), a university, or legislative body","a novice; one in the rudiments of knowledge"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/freshman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Freshman","blocks":[{"text":"A freshman, fresher, first year, or colloquially frosh, is a person in the first year at an educational institution, usually a secondary school or at the college and university level, but also in other forms of post-secondary educational institutions or primary school."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/1920_Locust_yearbook_p._095_%28Freshman%29.jpg/330px-1920_Locust_yearbook_p._095_%28Freshman%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freshman","wikidata":"Q13883551"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://